Hi all,

Is it possible to run a post hoc pairwise phylogenetic comparison of group means in Geomorph similar to the advanced.procD.lm function? I get a significant result for shape variation among groups using both the standard (Procrustes) and phylogenetic ANOVA, so now I would like to know which groups differ from each other. If it can't be run in a single command, could I simply set up the procD.pgls myself for each pairwise comparison? If so, can the groups be specified in the command line somehow or I would need to prune the data set for each comparison?

Thanks for any help,
Christy

