Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I want to quantify a plate-like structure on an insect thorax, and I have 3D mesh reconstructions from CT scans.  The plate is not easily segmented from the rest of the thorax, so I was hoping to place landmarks just on the plate and ignore the rest of the thorax.  Is there a way to assign surface sliding semilandmarks to a specific region of a 3D mesh rather than placing them evenly all over the surface?

I have assigned landmarks using Avizo and read their coordinates into Geomorph.  I tried making a template.txt file from one specimen’s landmarks (18 fixed plus 6 surface sliders) and then using digitsurface() to apply those landmarks to other surfaces, but the landmarks end up clumped together and in the wrong location - even on the surface from which I made the template.

I welcome any suggestions.

From uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com  Wed Sep 28 18:21:05 2016
From: uaab55242ff4da6c6 at groups.google.com (Michael Collyer)
Date: Wed, 28 Sep 2016 18:21:05 +0000
Subject: Re: [geomorph-r-package] pairwise phylogenetic test in Geomorph?
Message-ID: <wLLhEgjEPrE.NRMsgWfQAgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <wLLhEgjEPrE.i7xSLm6eAgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
References: <wLLhEgjEPrE.i7xSLm6eAgAJ@geomorph-r-package.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/geomorph-r-package/c/wLLhEgjEPrE/m/NRMsgWfQAgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Christy,

We do not currently have a function to do this, although we have one in development.  I know this is something you would like to do, but to date, nobody has examined the statistical properties of phylogenetic comparative methods (more generally and specifically, generalized least squares estimation) as applied to pairwise tests.  As soon as that happens in a formal way (the research is published), we will be eager to add such a function to our toolbox.

Because procD.pgls provides output that includes the phylogenetic correction (transformation) matrix, fitted values, residuals, and model design matrix, it is possible to create your own test for pairwise comparisons using the same elements we use in pairwise tests in advanced.procd.lm.  For example, one can randomize PGLS residuals and add them to PGLS fitted values in a permutation procedure, in order to generate distributions of pairwise differences.  This is logical, but again, we just do not know if such a procedure has appropriate statistical error rates.

Sorry this is not something we offer, but it is not because we have overlooked it - the theory just has not been developed yet.

Cheers!
Mike

